Expected elements: present

Identity bar carries the truncated hash, `Succeeded`, `block 63675`, four stepping groups, the `128 / 345` readout and the phase rail, and exits to `aztec-testnet`. There is no band above it, correctly. The provenance marker is the first row of the Transaction pane — `DATA`, a `Real Aztec testnet data` badge, and the capture's own sentences. All three source-less panes explain themselves in their own words; `Supply sources` is present; no file tab, line number or invented name anywhere.

Typographically the page is honest but under-ranked. Its most important claim is typeset exactly like `CANONICAL`: same 10px tracked uppercase label, same small badge, fourth in a run of ten identical rows — nothing in the type says this row is content and the rest is metadata. Worse, the provenance sentences inherit the value column's right alignment, so eleven lines of prose run ragged-left at a ~28-character measure: the one paragraph a reader must actually read is the hardest to read on the page. The same collapse hits section vs row (`DECODED INPUT` and `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` are styled as `SELECTOR` is), and the faithfulness evidence sits undifferentiated inside the raw JSON. Truncation strategy is applied in the identity bar (`0x0858d6…7fb2`) and abandoned in the pane, where a 64-character zero-padded fee prints in full across three lines.

Highest-priority fixes: left-align the provenance paragraph and widen its measure; give the `DATA` row and the section headers a second type level.

Rating: 6/10

